    "reasoning": "What the evidence shows: A QA tutor and a tutor each report that Submit stays grey after selecting B. A tutor reports being able to score both answers but getting no response when clicking Submit on task RP-1577. A QA tutor reports finishing the preference rubric but being unable to submit the pair on task RP-3325. A tutor reports completing every rubric field while the Submit button remains disabled. In each of the four threads, the team lead asks for the task ID, required-field state and exact button behavior, and states that submission status is still unverified. An engineer asks for the LT error state and time on tasks RP-3412 and RP-5337, stating that the wider cause is not confirmed in those threads. Current project instructions say to capture the task ID, required-field state, error and exact button behavior when Submit fails; a selected label is not a completed submission until LT confirms it. The earlier batch-15 handoff records disabled Submit reports after required fields were filled, an engineering handoff, and an open incident at the September 28 review, with no fix or successful submission recorded and no shared cause confirmed. The earlier browser-zoom review records two resolved batch-14 cases where Submit was below the visible area, not observed disabled; the proposed universal zoom FAQ remedy was rejected and not executed. A QA tutor asks whether required rating fields remain unset and whether the control is disabled; another QA tutor asks whether the interface shows a saved or submitted receipt rather than the same task again. Thread status, read from each thread's own messages: unresolved ×4. Agent 1's earlier labels (an input, not evidence): unresolved ×4; 2 of 4 were not verified by Agent 1. 3 advisor statements were not supported by the evidence and not shown.",
